data.multiwindowconfiguration#MultiWindowConf:
Ƭ MultiWindowConfiguration: Record<MultiWindowKey | "main-window", BrowserWindowConstructorOptions & { route?: string  }>Describes the configuration for multiple windows in an application, including the main window.
This type maps window identifiers (including 'main-window') to their respective configuration,
which includes standard BrowserWindow constructor options and an optional route.The route property can be used to specify the initial URL or frontend route the window should display.Example
const windowsConfig: MultiWindowConfiguration = {
  "main-window": { width: 800, height: 600, route: "/home" },
  "settings-window": { width: 600, height: 400, route: "/settings" }
};

